      "content": "exactly. it feels like we're losing the \"art\" part of art history. if we just accept that \"importance\" is the new metric for quality, aren't we basically admitting that art has become nothing more than a tool for propaganda or social activism? wouldn't you say that moving away from objective aesthetic standards actually makes art less meaningful in the long run?",
